STEP 7 -- designed: `rmon event` and `rmon alarm` put a real trap on the wire PASS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
awplus# configure terminal
awplus(config)# rmon event 11 log trap testing123 description ck44308rise owner ck44308
awplus(config)# rmon event 12 log trap testing123 description ck44308fall owner ck44308
awplus(config)# rmon alarm 11 etherStatsEntry.5.11 interval 10 delta rising-threshold 100 event 11 falling-threshold 10 event 12 alarmstartup 3 owner ck44308
awplus(config)# rmon alarm 12 etherStatsEntry.6.11 interval 10 delta rising-threshold 1 event 11 falling-threshold 1 event 12 alarmstartup 1 owner ck44308
awplus(config)# end

  Alarm 11 is the measurement.  It watches etherStatsPkts on port1.0.10, delta over 10 s,
  rising at 100.
  Alarm 12 is the control.  It is identical except that it watches etherStatsBroadcastPkts,
  which measured 0 in every earlier leg, and its startup type is 1 (rising only).  It must
  stay silent while alarm 11 fires.  It must still be able to fire when its own condition is
  met, which is why the sequence ends with 50 broadcast frames.

