STEP 9 -- designed: persistence across a reboot                               NOT RUN
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  This case did not reload the DUT and did not write to startup-config.  Persistence of the
  RMON configuration across a reboot is NOT MEASURED, and it is claimed nowhere in this log.
  The reason is the bench, not a choice about this case.  The layer 3 addresses this case
  needs -- `interface vlan10 10.38.22.34/27` on port1.0.10 -- exist in running-config only.
  The boot config is `flash:/default.cfg`, and it does not contain them.  A reload would
  therefore destroy the path to the SNMP manager and to the trap receiver.  Writing those
  addresses to startup-config would change the standing bench, which is never done unattended.
  => STEP 9 NOT RUN: a reload cannot be done on this bench without changing the standing
     configuration of the box.  Reboot persistence is left unmeasured.
